    "description": "",
    "h1": "How to Choose Between Hidden In Wall Speakers and Floor Standing Systems",
    "body": "- \n\n	How to Choose Between Hidden In Wall Speakers and Floor Standing Systems - Desert Sound\n	\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n- \n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n- \n\n## Blog\n\n- \n							                                \n- \n							                                \n- \n							                                \n- \n							                                \n- \n\n										                        SCROLL DOWN\n\n              by **admin**                        \n\n## How to Choose Between Hidden In Wall Speakers and Floor Standing Systems\n            June 15, 2026\n\nIf you're designing an excellent entertainment area for your home or a listening area that is a designated space, selecting the best audio equipment could be an enormous task. The choice of speakers can completely determine the look of your room as well as how much room you're able to move around in, and how realistic the music and movies sound. The design of homes is as crucial to audio technologies. This has led to a huge controversy between two distinct types of **sound systems** such as wall-mounted speakers that seamlessly blend into the architecture of your home as well as traditional floor standing models that sit prominently in your space as furniture pieces.\n\nMany homeowners are tangled between the two choices. The majority of them want their living spaces to appear neat, contemporary, sleek, and clutter-free, especially when integrating **home networking and Wifi systems**; however, they don't want to sacrifice the rich, powerful audio quality that brings their favourite audio and video content to life. Making the right choice for your family requires an understanding of the ways in which both systems function in conjunction with the room's boundaries, while your personal preferences determine the final purchase.\n\n## The Major Benefits of Choosing Hidden In Wall Speakers\n\nOne of the most evident and convincing reasons to opt for hidden wall speakers is its remarkable visual layout advantages. The traditional audio speaker is huge heavy wooden boxes that need an enormous amount of physical flooring space. They also come with a tangled collection of white speaker cables that dangle through your baseboards and carpets and create a messy look which can detract from the sleek design of a modern, minimalist living space. In-wall speakers can completely block out this visual hum. They're designed to sit in the standard space between the wall's wooden studs, enclosing all the wires safely behind the wall.\n\nOnce the speaker is installed the only visible component that the speaker has is an unflattering painted mesh grille that lies exactly flush with the wall. The grille can be painted to match the exact hue the walls are, rendering the speaker almost invisible to the untrained eyes. This neat setup can be a huge help for small apartments or living spaces that are multi-purpose in which maximising floor space for furniture and walking paths is the top priority. Also, keeping your speakers safely within the walls will protect the costly audio system from getting hit by a pet with a rage or vacuum cleaners by curious children.\n\n### Understanding the Trade-Offs in Sound Performance\n\nWhile in-wall speakers can be the ultimate triumph of the interior, they have some limitations in providing the highest quality audio. The sound is created through the motion of air. For deep, rich bass notes as well as warm mid-range vocals, speakers require a huge solid wooden enclosure that can manage the pressure waves that are created behind the moving cone. In wall speakers, they use the void, unsealed space in your drywall to serve as their enclosure. Since this wall cavity is unbraced, hollow and is shared along with other rooms in your home as well, the bass response may sometimes sound a little fragile, loose, or lacking in physical power.\n\nTraditional floor-standing speakers, commonly referred to as tower speakers, don't possess th",
